## Confirming the duplication

Read on all three files: the bodies are byte-identical apart from the local variable name (`working` / `cleaned` / `normalised`). The scan's `near_duplicate_block` (`crime_00002`, confidence 0.85) is correct — and on inspection the three are actually exact duplicates with renamed locals, not behaviourally divergent variants. There is no per-call configuration to thread through; one helper covers all three call sites.

The admin guards next to them (`assertAdminA/B/C`) are *deliberately* divergent (`role === "admin"`, `… || role === "owner"`, `role !== "admin"`) and feed `crime_00003` — they should **not** be folded into the sanitiser refactor.

## Refactor proposal

**Files that would change**

- `src/sanitize-a.ts` — delete `sanitizeUserInput`, keep `assertAdminA`, re-export `sanitize` as `sanitizeUserInput` for callers still using that name (or migrate them in the same PR).
- `src/sanitize-b.ts` — delete `sanitizeText`, keep `assertAdminB`, same re-export pattern.
- `src/sanitize-c.ts` — delete `cleanMessage`, keep `assertAdminC`, same re-export pattern.
- **New:** `src/sanitize.ts` — the single helper plus an exported options/limits type.

**Untouched:** `telemetry-a.ts`, `telemetry-b.ts`, `policy.ts`, the three `assertAdmin*` guards (separate finding — handle in a follow-up).

**Public API of the consolidated helper**

```ts
// src/sanitize.ts

export interface SanitizeLimits {
  /** Max length after whitespace collapse. Default: 1000. */
  maxLength?: number;
  /** Reject if 3+ consecutive !/? sequences appear more than this. Default: 5. */
  maxPunctuationBursts?: number;
  /**
   * Force lowercase when the uppercase ratio exceeds this AND the
   * string is at least `shoutMinLength` chars. Default: 0.9.
   */
  shoutUpperRatio?: number;
  /** Default: 30. */
  shoutMinLength?: number;
}

export function sanitize(
  input: string | null | undefined,
  limits?: SanitizeLimits,
): string;
```

Semantics match the existing body exactly: `null`/`undefined` → `""`, trim, strip space-hyphen, collapse whitespace, truncate at `maxLength`, reject leading `<`/`>`, reject `\x`, reject excess punctuation bursts, lowercase shouty inputs. Limits are optional with the current constants as defaults, so all three existing call sites can switch over with a one-token rename.

**Migration shape** (per old file):

```ts
// src/sanitize-a.ts
export { sanitize as sanitizeUserInput } from "./sanitize";
export function assertAdminA(role: string): boolean { return role === "admin"; }
```

That keeps the import surface for each old name stable for one release, after which the re-exports can be removed and callers updated to import `sanitize` directly.

